# An allow-list: everything is out unless named below. The image is the backend and the one
# frontend directory the backend reads at runtime (config.CIRCUIT_INDEX_PATH); a new runtime file
# outside backend/ needs a line here *and* a COPY in backend/Dockerfile.
*
!backend/
!frontend/data/circuits/

# …and, inside those, nothing that is only for development. backend/.env above all: a developer's
# real keys must never be baked into an image (CI plants a decoy to prove it). `.env*` also takes
# .env~, .env.local and .envrc, which hold the same keys.
**/.env*
backend/.venv
backend/tests
backend/scripts
backend/cache
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage*

# A local `fly deploy` builds from a working checkout, not a clean clone, so the gitignored clutter
# a checkout collects inside backend/ stays out too.
**/*~
**/*.log
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/venv
**/env
**/htmlcov
**/.mcp.json
**/.DS_Store
